    "title": "Clair Obscur: Expedition 33 — Part 5 — Gestral Village",
    "markdown": "# Clair Obscur: Expedition 33 — Part 5 — Gestral Village\r\n\r\n## EPISODE GOAL\r\n\r\nEvery village collectible, merchant exclusive, tournament, Manor record, and the Esquie's Nest password. Sciel joins.\r\n\r\n## STARTING POINT\r\n\r\nGestral Village Entrance Expedition Flag.\r\n\r\n## BEFORE WE START\r\n\r\n- **Weird Pictos** must be in inventory (Episode 1).\r\n- Bring Chroma. Buy every Colour of Lumina first at every stall.\r\n- Baguette / festival leftovers: if a Gestral offers a Baguette weapon for a Festival Token, spend a leftover token here or note the merchant for Episode 29.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## WALKTHROUGH\r\n\r\n### FROM: Gestral Village Entrance Expedition Flag\r\n\r\n☐ Activate.\r\n\r\n☐ **Left** toward arena signs.\r\n\r\n☐ At the final arena sign, small path **left of the sign**.\r\n\r\n# JOURNAL — Expedition 52\r\n\r\n**Area:** Gestral Village  \r\n**Nearest Flag:** Entrance  \r\n**Exact Directions:** arena-sign road, last sign, left spur  \r\n**When Available:** now\r\n\r\n☐ Do not enter the arena yet.\r\n\r\n### FROM: Entrance — right / TURN BACK\r\n\r\n☐ From the entrance, take paths **right** until a **TURN BACK** sign.\r\n\r\n☐ Ignore the sign. Go forward. Manor door.\r\n\r\n### The Manor — kitchen / dining record\r\n\r\n☐ Kitchen. Interact with three objects (PowerPyx):\r\n\r\n1. Small candlestick on the **left** table  \r\n2. Middle pan on the **right** wall  \r\n3. Statue to the right of that pan  \r\n\r\n☐ Floor hole opens. Drop. Loot the lower hall.\r\n\r\n☐ Stairs back up. Far door into the kitchen.\r\n\r\n☐ Opposite kitchen door → main Manor hall with the long table.\r\n\r\n☐ Interact with **four** wall decorations:\r\n\r\n1. Immediate **right** as you enter the hall  \r\n2. Far end, **back of a pillar**  \r\n3. **Left** side, round wall  \r\n4. **Left** side near the fireplace  \r\n\r\n☐ Hole opens under the last decoration.\r\n\r\n☐ Break boxes. **MUSIC RECORD — Nocturne pour un masque de tristesse**.\r\n\r\n# MUSIC RECORD — Nocturne pour un masque de tristesse\r\n\r\n**Area:** The Manor (entered from Gestral Village)  \r\n**Nearest Flag:** Village Entrance  \r\n**How Obtained:** 3 kitchen rotates + 4 dining decorations, box break  \r\n**Exact Directions:** TURN BACK sign path\r\n\r\n☐ Front door exits you back to the village.\r\n\r\n### Merchants and village extras\r\n\r\nWalk the village in a clockwise sweep from the entrance.\r\n\r\n☐ **Berrami** (journal Gestral, Bazar): talk. He pays Colour of Lumina for journals. Turn in everything you have (81, 68, 63, 52). Come back every episode you get journals.\r\n\r\n☐ Weird Pictos trader / village Gestral who recognises the unstable Picto:\r\n\r\n# PICTO — Augmented Aim\r\n\r\n**How to Obtain:** turn in Weird Pictos.  \r\n**Nearest Flag:** Entrance  \r\n**Recommended Characters:** Maelle, Verso later.\r\n\r\n☐ Casino / locked door at the far end: Gestral behind it. PowerPyx / MapGenie: first answer **Yes**, then follow his prompts. **VERIFY IN GAME** the exact dialogue. Take the reward (often a haircut or Picto).\r\n\r\n☐ Stage / dojo / shop Gestrals: buy **all Colour of Lumina**, then outfits/hair you do not own.\r\n\r\n☐ Merchant duel: accept every village duel. Rewards are finite.\r\n\r\n# MERCHANT DUEL — Gestral Village (each stall that offers one)\r\n\r\n**NG+ Expert Strategy:** Comfortable. Maelle First Strike.\r\n\r\n☐ Wooden Stick / kids / side skits: if a Gestral child gives a **Wooden Stick** quest item, take it. Used later in village / Golgra context. **VERIFY IN GAME** if the stick still exists on 1.5.5.\r\n\r\n### Tournament\r\n\r\n☐ Enter the arena when the village is empty of shops.\r\n\r\n☐ Fight the Gestral tournament (Sciel appears / joins through this sequence).\r\n\r\n# BOSS — Tournament Gestrals (multi-fight)\r\n\r\n**Type:** Story  \r\n**NG+ Expert Strategy:** Comfortable.  \r\n**Reward:** Sciel joins; Golgra audience; **password for Esquie's Nest**.\r\n\r\n# NEW PARTY — Sciel\r\n\r\n☐ Open her skill page. On NG+ she already has her kit. Equip Cheater / Painted Power / First Strike.\r\n\r\n### FROM: post-tournament village\r\n\r\n☐ Talk to **Golgra**. Get the Esquie's Nest password.\r\n\r\n☐ If a Gestral merchant appeared after the tournament, buy new stock.\r\n\r\n☐ Optional: Dark Gestral Arena / Hidden Gestral Arena — if the portal is already open on the Continent, it is usually a **later** difficulty spike. **GET NOW** only if you want the early fights; otherwise **RETURN LATER Episode 15/24**. Do not confuse it with the village arena.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## RETURN LATER CREATED\r\n\r\n| Item/Activity | Location | Reason | Unlock | Return |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| Paint Spikes in village alleys | Village | Paint Break | 4 Gestrals | 12 |\r\n| Golgra superboss | Village chief | She is not the tournament | Act III / high NG+ power | 24 (optional rematch) |\r\n| Hidden / Dark Gestral Arena | Continent | Difficulty / story | Esquie or later | 15 or 24 |\r\n| Berrami remaining journals | Bazar | Not found yet | Exploration | every episode |\r\n\r\n## NEWLY ACCESSIBLE CONTENT\r\n\r\nEsquie's Nest portal is now legal.\r\n\r\n## CAMP\r\n\r\n☐ Write Gustave's Journal.  \r\n☐ Talk to Sciel (first camp conversation if offered).  \r\n☐ Talk to Lune, Maelle.  \r\n☐ Sastro: if Gestral #1 is done and you skipped Episode 4 camp, take **Maelle Gestral hair** now.  \r\n☐ Play **Nocturne pour un masque de tristesse** and **Goblu**.\r\n\r\n## BUILD CHECK\r\n\r\n### Sciel\r\nWeapon: best carried Sciel weapon.  \r\nSkills: her card / Sun-Moon kit as you already built it.  \r\nLuminas: Cheater, Painted Power.  \r\n**Why:** she is the third body for Esquie's Nest / Francois.\r\n\r\n## EPISODE COMPLETION CHECK\r\n\r\n☐ JOURNAL — Expedition 52  \r\n☐ MUSIC RECORD — Nocturne pour un masque de tristesse  \r\n☐ Augmented Aim  \r\n☐ All village Lumina purchases  \r\n☐ All merchant duels  \r\n☐ Sciel in the party  \r\n☐ Esquie's Nest password  \r\n☐ Berrami paid for current journals\r\n\r\n## NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW\r\n\r\nEsquie's Nest. Francois. Esquie joins. Journal 66. Lost Gestral #1 if you still have not spoken to him.\r\n"
