    "title": "Clair Obscur: Expedition 33 — Part 12 — Paint Spike Backtrack",
    "markdown": "# Clair Obscur: Expedition 33 — Part 12 — Paint Spike Backtrack\r\n\r\n## EPISODE GOAL\r\n\r\nBreak every Paint Spike we have already walked past. Do not enter Monoco's Station. Do not start new story dungeons.\r\n\r\n## STARTING POINT\r\n\r\nCamp. Paint Break owned. Sastro's spike already broken (Episode 11).\r\n\r\n## BEFORE WE START\r\n\r\n- Strike / melee (`F` on PC, face-button melee on controller) breaks spikes. Shooting does not.\r\n- If a spike hides a path instead of an item, **walk the path** and take everything.\r\n- Spikes we have not seen yet (Old Lumière onward) are broken on first visit.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## WALKTHROUGH\r\n\r\nUse Continent flags / portals in this order. Fast-travel where the game allows.\r\n\r\n### FROM: Camp — Sastro\r\n\r\n☐ Confirm the camp spike is gone. If not, break it. **Colour of Lumina x1**.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Spring Meadows\r\n\r\n# FROM: Abandoned Expeditioner Camp\r\n\r\n☐ Face Jar. Right side. Break the spike.\r\n\r\n# PICTO — Aegis Revival\r\n\r\n**Exact Location:** right of Jar  \r\n**Nearest Flag:** Abandoned Expeditioner Camp  \r\n**How to Obtain:** Paint Break  \r\n**NG+ Expert Use:** revive-related; keep as Lumina if the text is a revive trigger.\r\n\r\n☐ Walk every other Spring Meadows flag (Meadows Corridor, Grand Meadow, Indigo Tree). Break any remaining blue clusters. Take Colour of Lumina / catalysts.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Flying Waters\r\n\r\n# FROM: Noco's Hut / Coral Cave / Lumieran Streets / Flower Field\r\n\r\n☐ Re-walk each flag. Break every spike in:\r\n\r\n- Entrance wreck bowl  \r\n- Demineur tunnel  \r\n- Coral Cave lower  \r\n- Lumieran Streets alleys  \r\n- Flower Field rim  \r\n\r\n☐ Typical rewards: Colour of Lumina, chroma, occasionally a Picto. **Name it in your head when you pick it up.** If a spike opens a ledge, fully clear the ledge.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Ancient Sanctuary\r\n\r\n# FROM: Entrance / Sanctuary Maze / Giant Bell Alley\r\n\r\n☐ Maze pockets and bell alley walls. Break all.\r\n\r\n☐ If a spike blocked a Sakapatate balcony, clear the balcony.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Gestral Village / Esquie's Nest\r\n\r\n# FROM: Village Entrance\r\n\r\n☐ Alleys behind stalls, casino rear, arena side rooms.\r\n\r\n# FROM: Esquie's Nest Entrance / Francois’ Cave\r\n\r\n☐ Nest sponge rooms and Francois approach.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Yellow Harvest / Lost Woods\r\n\r\n# FROM: Entrance / Harvester’s Hollow / Yellow Spire Wrecks\r\n\r\n☐ Hollow walls and wreck interiors.\r\n\r\n☐ Lost Woods: any rim spike.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Stone Wave Cliffs\r\n\r\n# FROM: Entrance / Paintress Shrine / Old Farm / Tide Caverns / Flooded Buildings / Basalt Waves\r\n\r\n☐ Farm, cavern, flooded rooms. This dungeon hid several spikes.\r\n\r\n☐ If a spike blocks a second Lune/Maelle pickup, take it.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Continent overworld spikes\r\n\r\n# FROM: Continent — ride Esquie around every portal we have used\r\n\r\nOverworld \"blue rocks\" you already smashed with Esquie were **not** Paint Spikes. Look for the smaller crystal clusters at portal mouths and on beaches we already landed on:\r\n\r\n- Esquie's Nest mouth  \r\n- Stone Wave Cliffs ramp  \r\n- White Tree island  \r\n- Meadows / Blades / Boat Graveyard beaches  \r\n- Gestral Beach mouths  \r\n\r\n☐ Break all. Colour of Lumina is the usual reward.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Forgotten Battlefield\r\n\r\n# FROM: Main Gate / Fort Ruins / Vanguard / Battlefield / Ancient Bridge\r\n\r\n☐ Trenches and fort. We left these because we did not have Paint Break.\r\n\r\n☐ If a spike blocks a Picto behind Dualliste, warp to Ancient Bridge and walk back.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Small Bourgeon / Twilight Quarry / Ancient Gestral City / Abbest Cave\r\n\r\n☐ Re-enter each tiny area. One spike each is common. Clear.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## RETURN LATER CREATED\r\n\r\nNone new. Every spike from Episodes 2–11 should now be **COMPLETED DURING EPISODE 12**.\r\n\r\nSpikes we have not visited:\r\n\r\n| Location | Return |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Monoco's Station / Frozen Hearts | 13 / 22 |\r\n| Old Lumière | 14 |\r\n| Falling Leaves / coral islands | 15 |\r\n| Sirène / Visages | 16–17 |\r\n| Monolith (including Random Defense lock behind a spike) | 19 |\r\n| Flying Manor / ENS / Drafts | 23–26 |\r\n\r\n## NEWLY ACCESSIBLE CONTENT\r\n\r\nOnly the spike rooms above.\r\n\r\n## CAMP\r\n\r\n☐ Sastro has no new Gestrals.  \r\n☐ Play any record you picked up inside spike rooms.  \r\n☐ Sleep if Maelle rank 1 has not fired — then it will.\r\n\r\n## BUILD CHECK\r\n\r\nSkip.\r\n\r\n## EPISODE COMPLETION CHECK\r\n\r\n☐ Aegis Revival  \r\n☐ Camp spike  \r\n☐ Spring Meadows / Flying Waters / Ancient Sanctuary / Village / Nest / Yellow Harvest / Stone Wave Cliffs / Forgotten Battlefield / Continent beaches all spike-cleared  \r\n☐ No new story flag pushed\r\n\r\n## NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW\r\n\r\nMonoco's Station. Monoco joins. Skill sweep begins.\r\n"
