    "title": "Clair Obscur: Expedition 33 — Part 21 — ESQUIE CAN FLY!",
    "markdown": "# Clair Obscur: Expedition 33 — Part 21 — ESQUIE CAN FLY!\r\n\r\n## EPISODE GOAL\r\n\r\nTurn flight on. Finish every relationship rank that does not need a long dungeon. Unlock **dive**. Take the easy flying journals/Gestrals/world bosses. Start Endless Tower Stages 1–3 only if you want. Long flying dungeons are Episodes 22–24.\r\n\r\n## STARTING POINT\r\n\r\nAct III camp after the Paintress.\r\n\r\n## BEFORE WE START\r\n\r\n- Painted Power on **every** character as a Lumina.\r\n- Cheater on the carry if you already own it.\r\n- Leave camp once if the story demands a cutscene, then **return to camp**. Do not fly to Lumière.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## WALKTHROUGH\r\n\r\n### CAMP — ranks 6–7 block\r\n\r\n# RELATIONSHIP EVENT — Esquie\r\n\r\n☐ Talk until rank 6. Francois 1v1 triggers.\r\n\r\n# BOSS — Francois (1v1)\r\n\r\n**Type:** Relationship  \r\n**Recommended Party:** whoever the game forces (usually Verso or the lead)  \r\n**NG+ Expert Strategy:** Strong Build — it is a solo.  \r\n**Reward:** **Urrie / dive**. Plane, Train, and Submarine achievement.\r\n\r\n☐ Talk to Esquie again to rank 7. **Verso Gradient: Angel's Eyes**.\r\n\r\n# RELATIONSHIP EVENT — Sciel\r\n\r\n☐ Talk to rank 6. **MUSIC RECORD — Sciel**.  \r\n☐ Talk to rank 7. **Sciel Gradient: End Slice**.  \r\n(If the record pops at 7 instead of 6, keep talking. See CONFLICTS.)\r\n\r\n# RELATIONSHIP EVENT — Lune\r\n\r\n☐ Rank 6 is gated by **Sirène's Dress**. Do that now.\r\n\r\n# FROM: Continent — fly to the **opposite** entrance of Sirène\r\n\r\n# OPTIONAL AREA — Sirène’s Dress\r\n\r\n**First Available:** fly  \r\n**Recommended Time:** now  \r\n**Difficulty:** Endgame Build Recommended (Chromatic inside)  \r\n**Why now:** Lune rank 6 + Journal 46 + Lune record.\r\n\r\n☐ Clear the area. Chromatic boss. Back of the area:\r\n\r\n# JOURNAL — Expedition 46\r\n\r\n☐ Return to camp. Finish Lune 6. **MUSIC RECORD — Lune**.  \r\n☐ Lune 7. **Lune Gradient: Sky Break**.\r\n\r\n# RELATIONSHIP EVENT — Monoco\r\n\r\n☐ Rank 6 is **Sacred River**. Do that after Sprong if Golgra feels ugly, or now on NG+.\r\n\r\n# FROM: Continent — fly north of Monoco's Station\r\n\r\n☐ Shop opposite the entrance: **MUSIC RECORD — Children of Lumière** (Citrelo, 1,000 Chroma).\r\n\r\n# OPTIONAL AREA — Sacred River\r\n\r\n☐ Pink Gestral apparition in the centre. **Golgra** vs Verso + Monoco.\r\n\r\n# BOSS — Golgra (Sacred River)\r\n\r\n**Type:** Relationship  \r\n**NG+ Expert Strategy:** Optimized / Endgame. Verso Steeled Strike while she is above half before she powers up (PowerPyx).  \r\n**Reward:** Monoco rank 6, **MUSIC RECORD — Monoco**.\r\n\r\n☐ Camp. Monoco 7. **Monoco Gradient: Break Point**.\r\n\r\n# RELATIONSHIP EVENT — Maelle\r\n\r\n☐ Rank 6 is **The Reacher** — Episode 22 (long dungeon). Do not start it this episode unless you are ahead.  \r\n☐ **Do not** do Maelle 7 until The Reacher is done. Rank 7 is **(TRUTH)** — Episode 22.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Easy flying pickups\r\n\r\n# FROM: Continent — fly west of Forgotten Battlefield, raised platform\r\n\r\n# JOURNAL — Julie\r\n\r\n# JOURNAL — Verso\r\n\r\nSame shelf. Tents vs back of the enemy group.\r\n\r\n# FROM: Continent — isolated grassy patch NE of The Reacher portal\r\n\r\n# LOST GESTRAL\r\n\r\n**World Location:** Reacher shelf  \r\n**Traversal:** fly  \r\n**Exact Directions:** IGN: boardwalk to The Reacher, turn right, isolated patch, face SE, Gestral by vases\r\n\r\n# FROM: Continent — south side of Endless Tower, high\r\n\r\n# LOST GESTRAL\r\n\r\n**World Location:** floating island S of Endless Tower  \r\n**Traversal:** fly  \r\n**Exact Directions:** fly up the south face of the tower, small island, only thing there\r\n\r\n# FROM: Continent — Grosse Tête\r\n\r\n# BOSS — Grosse Tête\r\n\r\n**Type:** World  \r\n**Monoco Skill:** Grosse Tete Whack  \r\n**NG+ Expert Strategy:** Strong Build. Bounce count increases; finish or parry until it explodes.  \r\n**1.5.5:** Gestral merchant near Grosse Tête sells **Anniversary haircuts** for Verso, Maelle, Lune, Sciel, Monoco. Buy all you do not own.\r\n\r\n# FROM: Continent — west of Blades' Graveyard, standing in the water\r\n\r\n# BOSS — Sprong\r\n\r\n**Type:** World  \r\n**Stages:** 1 all-hit → 2 debuffs → 3 five-hit → 4 charge → 5 Dark exterminate. Cycles harder.  \r\n**Reward:** **PICTO — Cheater**  \r\n**NG+ Expert Strategy:** Comfortable if you already have Cheater and are upgrading it. Superboss tag only if this is your first time on Expert without carry tools.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Endless Tower — optional opener\r\n\r\n# FROM: Continent — west/NW of Gestral Village, giant doorway\r\n\r\n☐ Under the **rightmost staircase**, north, glowing red: **Visages Outfit (Verso)** (1.5.0).\r\n\r\n☐ Stages 1–3 only if you want Greater Defenceless / Energising Rush / Clea haircut (Lune). Otherwise Episode 22/28.\r\n\r\n☐ Do **not** fight TY portraits yet except Chromatic Lampmaster if you want it early (original is dead).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Dive check\r\n\r\n☐ If Esquie 6 is done, dive is live. **Do not** start Verso's Drafts or Renoir's Drafts this episode. Episode 25.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## RETURN LATER CREATED\r\n\r\n| Item/Activity | Return |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| The Reacher + Maelle 6/7 | 22 |\r\n| Frozen Hearts | 22 |\r\n| Flying Manor / Clea | 24 |\r\n| Remaining tower | 22 / 28 |\r\n| Dive dungeons | 25–27 |\r\n| Lost Gestral #9 | 23 |\r\n\r\n## NEWLY ACCESSIBLE CONTENT\r\n\r\nFlight + dive (ability). Content spending continues 22–27.\r\n\r\n## BUILD CHECK\r\n\r\n### Everyone\r\nCheater + Painted Power. This is the Act III baseline.\r\n\r\n## CAMP\r\n\r\nAlready used as the spine of this episode.\r\n\r\n## EPISODE COMPLETION CHECK\r\n\r\n☐ Dive unlocked  \r\n☐ Records: Sciel, Lune, Monoco, Children of Lumière  \r\n☐ Journal 46, Julie, Verso  \r\n☐ Lost Gestrals #7 and #8  \r\n☐ Sprong / Cheater  \r\n☐ Grosse Tête + anniversary hairs  \r\n☐ Visages Outfit (Verso)  \r\n☐ Maelle 6 **not** finished unless you cheated ahead  \r\n☐ Lumière **not** entered\r\n\r\n## NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW\r\n\r\nThe Reacher (Maelle Truth), Frozen Hearts (Eternal Ice), first half of the flying dungeons.\r\n"
